## Color

Tokens live in `globals.css` as CSS custom properties. Never hardcode hex
values in components — reference the variable.

| Token              | Hex                      | Role                                                |
| ------------------ | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `--color-bone`      | `#F3F7FC` (v3, was `#FAFAF8`/`#171512`-dark surfaces) | Page-level surface (body, sections) — cool airy white |
| `--color-white`     | `#FFFFFF`                | Elevated card / product-tile surfaces (blended into glass) |
| `--color-ink`       | `#1B2737` (v3, was `#171512`) | Primary text — deep slate-ink                  |
| `--color-moss`      | `#2563EB` (v3, was `#455A38`) | Primary accent — CTAs, active nav, links (electric blue) |
| `--color-clay`      | `#C2410C` (v3, was `#B5602E`) | Secondary accent — sale tags, highlights (AA 4.9:1 on light) |
| `--color-stone`     | `#5B6B85` (v3, was `#8C8677`) | Muted text, secondary labels (WCAG AA 4.98:1 on bone) |

> **Legacy palette migration (v2 → v3):** v2 stored earthy hex values
> (`#171512` ink, `#FAFAF8` bone, `#CA8A04` amber, `#CDCCCA` link gray)
> directly in section/block rows. The section parsers (`lib/section-shared.ts`
> helpers `migrateSurfaceColor` / `migrateTextColor` / `migrateLinkHoverColor`
> / `migrateAccentColor`) remap those exact legacy values to the V3 palette at
> render time, role-aware — any merchant-customized color is left untouched.
> `prisma/seed.ts` already seeds V3 values for fresh databases.

**Rules:**
- Moss (blue) is the one accent allowed on primary CTAs. Never put moss and
  clay on the same CTA — clay is for badges/tags only, never buttons.
- Ink is a deep slate, not pure `#000`. Never substitute `#000000`.
- Max one accent-filled button per view. Everything else is outline/ghost.
- Page-level surfaces use `--color-bone`. Cards use the frosted glass surface
  (`--glass-bg` felted over the body's color glow) — the two read together as
  the classic light glassmorphism stack.
- Form inputs use a darker ink-based border (`rgba(27, 39, 55, 0.25)`), WCAG
  1.4.11. Focus state uses `--color-moss`.

## Glass system

v3 introduces a full glass layer (see the `--glass-*` tokens in
`globals.css`):

- **Page background:** `body` carries three fixed radial color glows
  (blue / violet / sky) — glass surfaces have something to blur.
- **Surfaces:** `rgba(255,255,255,0.62)` fill + `backdrop-filter:
  blur(16–20px) saturate(1.6)` + a 1px white hairline border (`--glass-border`)
  + soft blue-tinted glass shadows (`--shadow-glass`).
- **Utilities:** `.glass` (regular), `.glass-strong` (denser fill), and
  `.glass-edge` (inset top-edge light catch). The navbar uses an inline
  `color-mix(... 72%, transparent)` of the admin's background color with
  20px blur so an admin-chosen tint becomes the glass tint.

